(444032, 41046, 8860, '<td valign="top">Great contrast of environments, nice angle and lovely colours. Very intriguing structure too.<br/> <br/>One thing I''d take note of is hyperfocal length (it''s been in the forums - here''s a good link: //www.vividlight.com/articles/2314.htm). It would ensure that the distant subject is totally crisp (which this isn''t quite) as well as your foreground. Not a fatal flaw though - good work. [7]</td>', 'Great contrast of environments, nice angle and lovely colours. Very intriguing structure too. One thing I''d take note of is hyperfocal length (it''s been in the forums - here''s a good link: //www.vividlight.com/articles/2314.htm). It would ensure that the distant subject is totally crisp (which this isn''t quite) as well as your foreground. Not a fatal flaw though - good work. [7]', '2003-10-08 20:32:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(444034, 40738, 12618, '<td valign="top">Wow, that red sure sticks out.  Nice lines but a little overpowering maybe?</td>', 'Wow, that red sure sticks out.  Nice lines but a little overpowering maybe?', '2003-10-08 20:33:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(444035, 40800, 8860, '<td valign="top">... Metaphorically speaking I assume!  Very atmospheric, and the thumbnail almost looks like a building poking out of a hazy city. Lovely shot. [7]</td>', '... Metaphorically speaking I assume!  Very atmospheric, and the thumbnail almost looks like a building poking out of a hazy city. Lovely shot. [7]', '2003-10-08 20:33:31.000000', NULL, 1),
