(451264, 41404, 3419, '<td valign="top">I''m actually surprised that this photo placed and scored as well as it did. I know the colors are muted and there''s not much contrast, but this is how the scene actually looked. The washout in the sky is actually the haze of pollution from Toronto, and the dark smudge in the top left corner is dust inside my camera. To take this shot, I climbed to the top of a construction site hill of dirt. And how coincidental - just yesterday on the VR 6:00 news, they had a story about the danger of urban sprawl to our environment.</td>', 'I''m actually surprised that this photo placed and scored as well as it did. I know the colors are muted and there''s not much contrast, but this is how the scene actually looked. The washout in the sky is actually the haze of pollution from Toronto, and the dark smudge in the top left corner is dust inside my camera. To take this shot, I climbed to the top of a construction site hill of dirt. And how coincidental - just yesterday on the VR 6:00 news, they had a story about the danger of urban sprawl to our environment.', '2003-10-15 11:42:13.000000', NULL, 0),
