(737517, 40754, 22192, '<td valign="top">I really enjoy this one - showing how empty LA is at night.  One suggestion - your "(cheezy) tripod" sort of made a small earthquake on the right side - what if you cropped in on both sides to make it a "portait" shot instead of "landscape"?  It would also help emphasize the verticality of the open space between the builidings at the end of the road.  Might also lend some of the "big city" "skyscraper" feel which, of course, LA has very little of (none, compared to NYC!).<br/> <br/>Awsome exposure and colors!</td>', 'I really enjoy this one - showing how empty LA is at night.  One suggestion - your "(cheezy) tripod" sort of made a small earthquake on the right side - what if you cropped in on both sides to make it a "portait" shot instead of "landscape"?  It would also help emphasize the verticality of the open space between the builidings at the end of the road.  Might also lend some of the "big city" "skyscraper" feel which, of course, LA has very little of (none, compared to NYC!). Awsome exposure and colors!', '2004-05-26 14:28:54.000000', NULL, 0),
